       qs : Index\n1458 |             The quantiles to be computed in float64.\n1459 |         interpolation : str, default 'linear'\n1460 |             Type of interpolation.\n1461 | \n1462 |         Returns\n1463 |         -------\n1464 |         Block\n1465 |         \"\"\"\n1466 |         # We should always have ndim == 2 because Series dispatches to DataFrame\n1467 |         assert self.ndim == 2\n1468 |         assert is_list_like(qs)  # caller is responsible for this\n1469 | \n1470 |         result = quantile_compat(self.values, np.asarray(qs._values), interpolation)\n1471 |         # ensure_block_shape needed for cases where we start with EA and result\n1472 |         #  is ndarray, e.g. IntegerArray, SparseArray\n1473 |         result = ensure_block_shape(result, ndim=2)\n1474 |         return new_block_2d(result, placement=self._mgr_locs)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/managers.py:BlockManager.quantile`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1637 | def quantile(\n1638 |         self,\n1639 |         *,\n1640 |         qs: Index,  # with dtype float 64\n1641 |         interpolation: QuantileInterpolation = \"linear\",\n1642 |     ) -> Self:\n1643 |         \"\"\"\n1644 |         Iterate over blocks applying quantile reduction.\n1645 |         This routine is intended for reduction type operations and\n1646 |         will do inference on the generated blocks.\n1647 | \n1648 |         Parameters\n1649 |         ----------\n1650 |         interpolation : type of interpolation, default 'linear'\n1651 |         qs : list of the quantiles to be computed\n1652 | \n1653 |         Returns\n1654 |         -------\n1655 |         BlockManager\n1656 |         \"\"\"\n1657 |         # Series dispatches to DataFrame for quantile, which allows us to\n1658 |         #  simplify some of the code here and in the blocks\n1659 |         assert self.ndim >= 2\n1660 |         assert is_list_like(qs)  # caller is responsible for this\n1